\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\par
\b0  \par
\ul\b Task1 b\ulnone\b0\par
\ul\b Algorithm \ulnone\b0 DFS \f1\endash\par
Step 1: Declare a queue and insert the starting Vertex.\par
Step 2: Initialize a visited array and mark the starting Vertex as visited.\par
Step3: Remove the First vertex of queue.\par
Step 4: Mark that vertex as visited\par
Step 5: Insert all the unvisited neighbors of the vertex into queue.\par
Step 6: stop.\par
Program\par
from collections import deque \par
def dfs(graph, start):\par
stack, visited = [start], set() \par
print("DFS:", end=" ") \par
while stack:\par
node = stack.pop()\par
if node not in visited: \par
print(node, end=" ") \par
visited.add(node)\par
stack.extend(reversed([neighbor for neighbor in graph[node] if neighbor not in visited])) \par
print()\par
\b # Example graph \par
graph = \{\par
 1: [2, 3],\par
 2: [4, 5],\par
 3: [6],\par
 4: [],\par
 5: [],\par
 6: []\par
\}\par
dfs(graph, 1)\par
Output:\par
DFS: 1 2 4 5 3 6\par

